Wine 11.18 exported renderer bounds and asynchronous geometry recovery.

Use the actual current client rectangle for the retained exported CAMetalLayer,
not only its construction-time bounds. Cocoa updates/readback run on main;
NT/USER work and the confirmed/uncertain cache stay on Wine recovery threads.
Invalidate the cache before an operation which can partially apply and throw.
Do not replace a device/context/swapchain or release on advisory notification.

SetParent/WindowPosChanged post a coalesced wake to the existing PE dispatcher,
outside the service lock. Cocoa never posts NT work; known post failures keep
the periodic recovery fallback. No per-frame USER work or wire/table changes.
Normal TRACE observations report route handoff/retirement and confirmed bounds;
these do not certify all callback tails, global GPU idle or physical scanout.

Experimental route only; local-default and game policy adoption remain gated.

